# Your lab settings. Copy this file to lab.env (Git ignores lab.env, so keys stay on your
# machine), uncomment what you need, then run ./lab.sh ai to store the AI settings in the
# cluster. The file is read by bash, so quote a value that has spaces or special characters.
#
# Without lab.env the AI modules (17, 18, 19 and 27) use Ollama on your machine with qwen2.5:3b.

# --- The language model the AI apps call (module 17's assistant, module 27's RAG app)
# LLM_PROVIDER picks the API: ollama (Ollama's own API), openai (any OpenAI-compatible
# server: Ollama's /v1, vLLM, LM Studio, OpenAI, Grok, Gemini, Groq, OpenRouter) or anthropic.
# Pods reach your machine as host.docker.internal, never as localhost.

# Ollama on your machine, through its own API (the default):
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# LLM_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
# LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b

# Ollama on your machine, through its OpenAI-compatible endpoint:
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b

# A hosted OpenAI-compatible provider (the URL ends in /v1 or the provider's equivalent):
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-5-mini
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...

# Claude through the Anthropic API (see docs/ai-models.md for the mesh setup in module 17):
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# LLM_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- Embeddings for module 27's search
# With LLM_PROVIDER=openai the RAG app asks the same server's /embeddings endpoint; otherwise
# it asks Ollama. Set these when your chat provider has no embedding model.
# EMBED_PROVIDER=ollama
# EMBED_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
# EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
# EMBED_API_KEY=

# --- The ollama service in compose.yaml (./lab.sh ollama), for machines without Ollama
# LAB_OLLAMA_MODELS="qwen2.5:3b nomic-embed-text"
# LAB_OLLAMA_PORT=11434         # another port when something else uses 11434
# LAB_OLLAMA_BIND=0.0.0.0       # needed on Linux, where pods reach the host through its gateway
